===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*wedʰ-}}
From {{der|en|enm|wage}}, from {{der|en|xno|wage}}, from {{der|en|fro-nor|wage}}, a northern variant of {{der|en|fro|gauge}}, {{m|fro|guage}} (whence modern French {{m|fr|gage}}), {{der|en|ML.|wadium}}, from {{der|en|frk|*wadi|*waddī}} (cognate with {{cog|ang|wedd}}), from {{der|en|gem-pro|*wadją||pledge}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*wedʰ-||to pledge, redeem a pledge}}. Akin to {{cog|non|veðja||to pledge}}, {{cog|got|𐍅𐌰𐌳𐌹}}, {{cog|nl|wedde}}. Compare also the doublet {{m|en|gage}}. More at {{m|en|wed}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|often in plural}} An amount of money paid to a worker for a [[specify|specified]] quantity of [[work]], usually calculated on an hourly basis and expressed in an amount of money per hour.
#:{{ux|en|Before her promotion, her '''wages''' were 20% less.}}

